00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:29.280
In a casual modern use TradCath tends to&nbsp;
just refer to a particularly conservative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:34.160
strain of Catholic thinker, but Robert&nbsp;
is a bit more of a traditional TradCath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:38.080
which means he errs a lot more towards&nbsp;
the philosophical roots of the term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:43.760
which is rooted in opposition to the&nbsp;
Second Vatican Council, AKA Vatican II.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:50.000
Held between 1959 and 1965, this was a series&nbsp;
of formal debates within the Catholic church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:54.320
in direct response to a number of&nbsp;
internal and external pressures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.040
such as the growing Civil&nbsp;
Rights Movement in America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.040 --> 00:21:02.480
Women’s Liberation, declining Church attendance,&nbsp;
the evangelical/nondenominational movement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:08.720
and growing criticism and scrutiny. It was, in&nbsp;
short, an attempt at modernizing the church.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:13.280
These sessions resulted in a number of&nbsp;
substantial changes to church operations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.760
general policy, logistical changes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:21.360
and official redefinition of the relationship&nbsp;
between the church and various social groups.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:24.640
Among the more obvious and dramatic&nbsp;
changes were that it became formally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:27.920
permitted for Mass to be administered&nbsp;
in a language that wasn’t Latin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:35.680
and encouraged a greater emphasis on&nbsp;
lay-participation rather than strict clerical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:41.280
dispensation. This means, one, getting general&nbsp;
congregants more involved in weekly services&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:46.240
and, two, actually performing Mass in the&nbsp;
language that the congregation speaks.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:51.440
This is also when the church formally changed&nbsp;
its opinion on the death of Jesus, stating

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.920
“True, the Jewish authorities and those&nbsp;
who followed their lead pressed for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.920 --> 00:22:01.440
death of Christ; still, what happened in His&nbsp;
passion cannot be charged against all the Jews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:07.520
without distinction, then alive, nor against&nbsp;
the Jews of today. Although the Church is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:13.200
new people of God, the Jews should not be&nbsp;
presented as rejected or accursed by God.”

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:18.320
So they no longer held all Jews categorically&nbsp;
responsible for the death of Jesus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:25.040
Which they previously had for hundreds&nbsp;
and hundreds and hundreds of years.

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:26.880
I guess better late than never.

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:31.520
The last change I want to mention was the church&nbsp;
pivoting its view on non-Catholic Christian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:37.120
denominations, reverting the anti-Reformation&nbsp;
Council of Trent, viewing protestants and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:43.200
Eastern Orthodox tradition specifically as&nbsp;
“separated brethren” rather than heretics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:48.560
This is a subtle but important policy change&nbsp;
because it effectively signaled that the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:53.760
traditionalist denominations shared common&nbsp;
political interests and it would be more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:59.280
important to cooperate on those fronts&nbsp;
than hold onto old sectarian grudges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:04.640
but in doing so the church ceded its&nbsp;
absolute stance of supreme authority.

00:23:04.640 --> 00:23:10.880
So this is complicated. Vatican II is, in some&nbsp;
regards, progressive, but only as progressive as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:16.560
needed to retain membership and improve political&nbsp;
relations with other conservative organizations.

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.040
So imagine the kind of person&nbsp;
who thinks it was going too far.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:27.520
Now, in all fairness Sungenis has stated in a 2005&nbsp;
